  "shipped": "painted",
  "variant": 1,
  "why": "orch1 W3-B ruling 56: rebuilt brow-visor model, painted v1 passes every gate; calm open eyes with pupils by eye at full, 128 and 64 px",
  "model": "grok-imagine-image",
  "prompt_version": 9,
  "prompt": "Repaint this exact image as one finished, hand-painted fantasy game key-art illustration: painterly brushwork with soft and lost edges over the figure and the landscape alike, painted form and light, a rich value structure. Keep the composition, the camera, the framing, the background layout and the character's pose, silhouette, proportions, costume parts and colours exactly as in the reference. Do not add or remove props, limbs or figures; do not move, turn or resize the character. Add no colour, ornament, band or part that is not in the reference. Paint only what is visible in the reference: anything described below that is out of frame stays out of frame. Add no object, light source, sun disc, lens or prop that the reference does not show. Keep the reference's overall brightness and the background's value; do not brighten the image. A wide 16:9 splash card. The character: a lean runner: a slim smoked amber glass brow visor band across the forehead above a carved pale face-plate, two swept-back pale crest plates with a small lamp cage on the crest, walnut-light pauldrons and forearm guards, a warm brown tabard, a pale scarf, walnut leather straps, dark walnut shin plates and boots, holding two long glass knives in reverse grip. The face-plate under the visor is carved and alive, never a blank white oval, a doll or a mannequin: keep its carved brow, nose and eyes exactly as rendered, with no marks, lines, cracks or streaks under the eyes. The nose is a smooth carved ridge with no nostril holes; no sunken cheeks, no deep round eye sockets, no cracked or aged surface: never a skull. Light: a low warm golden sun from the right, a warm rim light along the character's right edges, cooler shadow on the far side, a soft shadow cast from the feet onto the ground they stand on. Eyes: below the glass brow visor, on the face-plate, two calm open almond eyes exactly where the reference shows them: a muted white, a steel-blue iris with a dark pupil, a heavy calm upper lid with a dark lash line; never glowing, never hollow or empty, never a blank plate, no bright or saturated ring. The face-plate is warm pale stone with soft painted shading on the far cheek, a carved nose ridge and a small calm closed mouth; no lines, grooves or streaks on the cheeks; below the visor two calm open eyes with lids, a steel-blue iris and dark pupils, readable at a glance; the visor is a slim glass band over the brow only, never over the eyes and never a beak in front of the face. No glyphs or letter-like marks anywhere. Hands: gloved hands with separate fingers, knuckles and a thumb exactly as in the reference, each finger where it is rendered; never a mitten, a block or fused fingers. Painted form, not a 3D render; no outline halo. No text, no letters, no logo, no signature, no border, no frame. Sensitivity: no blank, smooth, cracked or skull-like masks, no hockey masks, no mannequin faces, no empty or glowing eye holes, no glowing eyes; no animal ears, no full-head cowls, no capes, no skull plates, no horns; no tall, pointed or conical hoods (any hood is soft, low and rounded); no faceless crowds, no armies or rows of small soldiers, no little figures with faces on the roads; nothing that resembles a character from another game, film or comic.",
